From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: add the SM8350 C-PHY sequence

The SM8350 CSIPHY is revision 1.2.3. Add its three-phase settings, taken
entry by entry from the downstream camera driver in the Galaxy Z Flip3
kernel source (techpack/camera, cam_csiphy_1_2_3_hwreg.h): the per-trio
table csiphy_3ph_v1_2_3_reg, preceded by the common CTRL7 value 0x5a,
which overrides the generic 0x02 just as in the two-phase table. The
two-phase-only CTRL9 write is not part of it.

Unlike the two-phase table, the three-phase one never programs the
settle count. Downstream writes it, together with a few receiver
settings, from a second table that depends on the data rate
(data_rate_delta_table_1_2_3). Its tiers cover up to 2.5, 3.5 and
4.5 Gsps per trio. Add a helper that picks the tier from the symbol
rate, which on a C-PHY link is twice the link frequency, and writes it
after the base table, in the same order as downstream. Downstream gives
the tier limits in bits per second (Gsps x 2.28); here they are stored
as symbols per second. Where downstream has a different 0x980 value for
another device, the generic 0x60 is used.

The lane enable value downstream writes for three-phase, 0x2a, is what
csiphy_get_lane_mask() computes for trios 0, 1 and 2.

The settle count high byte entries write their table value, 0, as the
settle count is a u8. csiphy_gen2_config_lanes() now calls a helper with
the same loop, so the D-PHY register writes do not change.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
